  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Potential for frost tonight and Wednesday night\nacross the north.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nHigh pressure will continue to build in throughout this \nafternoon and overnight tonight, resulting in favorable \nradiational cooling conditions as low lying valleys decouple. \nPatchy/areas of frost and fog are expected tonight and again \nWednesday night in northern areas with temperatures dipping to \nnear and below freezing each night in normally colder low lying \nand valley locations.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A coastal low could impact at least Downeast\nMaine late this week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nA coastal low is expected to develop across the Mid-Atlantic\nregion later this week while high pressure remains centered over\nQuebec. The track of the ocean low is still uncertain with \nblocking high pressure to the northwest of our forecast area and\nridging across the Great Lakes. Uncertainty remains regarding \nthe northern edge of the precipitation shield and whether rain \nwill reach Downeast Maine. Northerly to northeasterly winds \ncould become gusty over the weekend, especially along the coast,\nas a tight pressure gradient forms. General trend currently is\nthat the low pressure system will continue to move southwards\ndue to the high pressure, with majority of the rain staying \nover waters and immediate coast.",
